      "Put <code>HatSize_FX</code> in the <code>Controller</code> field of the <code>Animator</code> on the top of your avatar, only while you record. Choose <code>Hat_Size</code> in the Animation window and click the record button.",
      "Check that the frame field (the number to the right of the play button) is 0. Select <code>Hat</code> in the Hierarchy, and in the Inspector, set the Transform's <code>Scale</code> to 0.5 for X, Y, and Z.",
      "Type 60 in the frame field to move to frame 60. Set <code>Scale</code> to 1.5 for X, Y, and Z. Stop recording.",
      "Click <code>Curves</code> at the bottom of the Animation window, select all the keys, right-click, and choose <code>Both Tangents → Linear</code>. Now the value changes at a steady rate between the keys. (If you leave it as is, it may become a curve that changes slowly near the ends.)",
      "Select <code>Hat_Size</code> in the Project window and uncheck <code>Loop Time</code> in the Inspector. If it stays checked, the very end (1) may look like it jumps back to the starting shape.",
      "Check that the Scale of <code>Hat</code> is back to how it was before recording, and put the <code>Controller</code> field of the <code>Animator</code> back.",
    ],
    floatColor: "Changing color works the same way. At frames 0 and 60, add keys on the material's color row (a row like <code>Mesh Renderer : Material._Color</code>. The name depends on the shader).",
    floatMenuTitle: "Hook it up to your avatar and add it to the menu",
    floatMenu: [
      "To hook it up with MA, make an object named <code>Hat Size</code>, and add MA Merge Animator (<code>HatSize_FX</code>) and MA Parameters. Add <code>HatSize</code> as a <code>Float</code>, set <code>Default Value</code> to 0.5 (which is Scale 1.0), and check <code>Saved</code> and <code>Synced</code>.",
      "Add MA Menu Installer and MA Menu Item, and set <code>Type</code> to <code>Radial Puppet</code>. Put <code>HatSize</code> in the field for the value you turn (the field labeled Rotation).",
      "In VRChat, pressing this item opens a dial. Turning it changes HatSize from 0 to 1.",
    ],
    btTitle: "Another way: Blend Tree (1D)",
    btLead: "A Blend Tree blends several clips together based on a parameter's value. You can use it instead of Motion Time.",
    bt: [
      "In the Project window, make two empty clips: <code>Hat_Small</code> and <code>Hat_Big</code>.",
      "Right-click an empty spot in the <code>HatSize</code> layer and choose <code>Create State → From New Blend Tree</code>. You'll use it instead of the Motion Time state, so right-click it and choose <code>Set as Layer Default State</code>.",
      "Double-click the new state to see the <code>Blend Tree</code> inside. Click it.",
      "In the Inspector, set <code>Blend Type</code> to <code>1D</code> and <code>Parameter</code> to <code>HatSize</code>.",
      "Choose <code>Add Motion Field</code> twice from the <code>+</code> under <code>Motion</code>, and put in <code>Hat_Small</code> and <code>Hat_Big</code>.",
      "Uncheck <code>Automate Thresholds</code>, and set the Threshold to 0 for <code>Hat_Small</code> and 1 for <code>Hat_Big</code>.",
      "Record the same way as above: a Scale 0.5 key in <code>Hat_Small</code> and a Scale 1.5 key in <code>Hat_Big</code>, only at frame 0. The Blend Tree blends between them, so you don't need to set the keys to Linear.",
    ],
    btWhen: [
      "<strong>Which to use</strong>: Motion Time needs only one clip, so it's quicker to build. A Blend Tree is a better fit when you also want to set the shape in the middle (three shapes: small at 0, normal at 0.5, and big at 1), or when you want to keep the clips separate.",
      "Blend Trees work when the parameter is a Float. VRChat may convert the value when the type differs between Expression Parameters and the Animator. For example, you can make it a Bool in Expression Parameters, and use the same name as a Float in the Animator for a Blend Tree.",
    ],
    demoTitle: "Try it out",
    demoLead: "Move the value as if you were turning a Radial Puppet. With Motion Time, you'll see which point in the 60-frame clip is used, and how the hat looks.",
    demo: {
      look: "How it looks",
      clip: "Position in the clip",
      slider: "Radial Puppet value (HatSize)",
      mode: "What the clip changes",
      modes: [
        { value: "size", text: "Size (Scale 0.5 → 1.5)" },
        { value: "color", text: "Color (blue → red)" },
      ],
      frame: "HatSize is {v}, so the value at frame {f} of the 60-frame clip is used.",
      size: "The hat's Scale is {x}.",
      color: "The hat's color is {p}% of the way from blue to red.",
      remote: "Others receive about {r} (because it's rounded to 8 bits).",
      noJs: "Turn on JavaScript to use this demo.",
    },
    syncTitle: "Sync, precision, and how others see it",
    sync: [
      "<strong>Bool and Int values reach others exactly.</strong> If OutfitNo is 2, it's 2 on other people's screens too.",
      "<strong>Float values are rounded to 8 bits when they're sent to others.</strong> The range from -1 to 1 is split into about 255 steps, so each step is about 1/127. 0.503 on your screen might be 0.504 for others. For size or color, you'll hardly notice.",
      "Values arrive a little late. If you turn the dial quickly, others may see it lag behind, or change in steps.",
      "The official docs say that while a dial (like a Radial Puppet) is open and you're turning it, the value is sent often and smoothed out on the other person's side. But how smooth it looks depends on things like the connection. <strong>The value you end on does reach others.</strong> It's safest to assume the motion in between won't look exactly the same.",
      `For the detailed rules, see ${ext(links.params, "VRChat's Animator Parameters page")}.`,
    ],
    bitsTableLabel: "Examples of the sync cost of the parameters used in this tip and the previous one",
    bitsHead: ["Parameter", "Type", "Sync cost"],
    bitsRows: [
      ["HatOn", "Bool", "1 bit"],
      ["OutfitNo", "Int", "8 bits"],
      ["HatSize", "Float", "8 bits"],
      ["Total", "", "17 bits (up to 256 bits allowed)"],
    ],
    bits: [
      "Parameters with Synced unchecked use none of the budget. Instead, others keep seeing the Default. Use this for things only you need to see.",
      "If you go over 256 bits, you can't upload. Places like the Expression Parameters Inspector show how much you're using.",
    ],
    casesTitle: "Common problems and fixes",
    caseLabels: { symptom: "What happens", cause: "Cause", fix: "Fix" },
    cases: [
      { title: "Two outfits show at once",
        symptom: "You picked a different outfit, but the previous one doesn't go away, and they overlap.",
        cause: "The clip has no rows for the other outfits (Is Active at 0). Write Defaults is OFF, so the previous value stays.",
        fix: "Put Is Active rows for all three outfits in every clip, from Outfit_0 to Outfit_3." },
      { title: "Picking an outfit doesn't switch anything",
        symptom: "You press an outfit in the menu, but nothing changes.",
        cause: "The Animator parameter's name or type (Int) is different, or the Equals number on an arrow from Any State is wrong. The layer's Weight may also be 0.",
        fix: "Match the name and type between MA Parameters and the Animator. Check that the arrows' numbers match the menu's Values." },
      { title: "A clip with motion keeps playing from the start",
        symptom: "You added an animation like swaying to an outfit, but it looks stuck in its first pose.",
        cause: "Can Transition To Self is checked on the arrows from Any State. The layer re-enters the state every frame.",
        fix: "Uncheck Can Transition To Self on every arrow from Any State." },
      { title: "Turning the dial doesn't change the size",
        symptom: "You turn the Radial Puppet, but the hat's size doesn't change.",
        cause: "Parameter isn't checked on the state's Motion Time, or the clip only has a key at frame 0.",
        fix: "Check Motion Time and choose HatSize. Add keys at both frame 0 and the end of the clip." },
      { title: "At the largest size, it snaps back to small",
        symptom: "When you turn the dial all the way, the hat takes its smallest shape.",
        cause: "Loop Time is checked on the clip, so the end connects back to the start.",
        fix: "Select the clip in the Project window and uncheck Loop Time in the Inspector." },
      { title: "It changes fast in the middle and slowly at the ends",
        symptom: "It doesn't change as much as you turn, and barely changes near the ends.",
        cause: "The curve between the keys flattens out at the ends.",
        fix: "In the Animation window, open Curves and select the keys. Right-click and choose Both Tangents → Linear." },
      { title: "It looks late to others",
        symptom: "It changes smoothly for you, but a friend says it looks late and changes in steps.",
        cause: "Float values arrive a little late over the network, and they're rounded to 8 bits.",
        fix: "This is normal. If the value you end on matches, it's fine. If you want to show fast motion, build it so the clip itself plays, instead of turning a Float." },
    ],
    careTitle: "Things to watch out for",
    care: [
      "When you switch with an Int, put rows for everything you switch in every clip.",
      "Uncheck Can Transition To Self on arrows from Any State.",
      "For clips used with Motion Time, uncheck Loop Time and add keys at the start and the end.",
      "Floats are rounded to 8 bits and reach others a little late. For things that need exactly the same value, split them into steps with an Int.",
      "The sync budget is 256 bits for the whole avatar. Parameters added by other tools, like outfit gimmicks, count too.",
      "To change size, move the Scale of the accessory object, not Humanoid bones.",
    ],
    sumTitle: "Summary",
    sum: [
      "Use Bool for on/off, Int to pick one of several, and Float to change things gradually.",
      "With an Int, move to each state from Any State with an Equals condition. Uncheck Can Transition To Self.",
      "A menu Toggle sets its Value when on, and 0 when off. Make one item for each value, and only one can be picked.",
      "Turn a Float with a Radial Puppet, and use the state's Motion Time to turn it into a position in the clip. You can also build it with a Blend Tree.",
      "Floats are rounded to 8 bits and reach others a little late.",
    ],
    next: `In the next tip, ${tipLink("gesture")}, you'll switch facial expressions with hand gesture numbers.`,
    back: "All Avatar Tips",
  },
}[pageLocale];
const sections = [
  { id: "when", title: l.whenTitle },
  { id: "choose", title: l.chooseTitle },
  { id: "int", title: l.intTitle },
  { id: "float", title: l.floatTitle },
  { id: "demo", title: l.demoTitle },
  { id: "sync", title: l.syncTitle },
  { id: "cases", title: l.casesTitle },
  { id: "care", title: l.careTitle },
  { id: "summary", title: l.sumTitle },
];
const d = l.demo;
const v0 = 0.5;
const fill = (text, values) => text.replace(/\{(\w)\}/g, (m, key) => (key in values ? String(values[key]) : m));
%><article class="article_1" aria-labelledby="article-heading">
  <header class="section_2 page_1 article_1__header">
    <p class="article_1__series"><a href="<%= prefix %>/avatar-tips/"><%= l.series %></a></p>
    <h1 class="page_1__h1" id="article-heading"><%= l.title %></h1>
    <p class="article_1__lead"><%= l.lead %></p>
    <p class="section_2__note"><%= l.publishedLabel %> <time datetime="<%= article.published %>"><%= published %></time> · <%= l.meta %></p>
    <nav class="jump_1" aria-label="<%= l.tocLabel %>">
      <ul>
        <% sections.forEach(function (s) { %>
          <li><a href="#<%= s.id %>"><%= s.title %></a></li>
        <% }); %>
      </ul>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <section class="section_2 article_1__section" id="when" aria-labelledby="when-heading">
    <h2 class="section_2__h1" id="when-heading"><%= l.whenTitle %></h2>
    <ul class="rules_1">
      <% l.when.forEach(function (item) { %><li><%= item %></li><% }); %>
    </ul>
    <p class="article_1__p"><%- l.before %></p>
  </section>

  <section class="section_2 article_1__section" id="choose" aria-labelledby="choose-heading">
    <h2 class="section_2__h1" id="choose-heading"><%= l.chooseTitle %></h2>
    <p class="article_1__p"><%- l.chooseLead %></p>
    <section class="table_3" tabindex="0" aria-label="<%= l.chooseTableLabel %>">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><% l.chooseHead.forEach(function (h) { %><th scope="col"><%= h %></th><% }); %></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <% l.chooseRows.forEach(function (row) { %>
            <tr><th scope="row"><%= row[0] %></th><% row.slice(1).forEach(function (cell) { %><td><%= cell %></td><% }); %></tr>
          <% }); %>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>
    <ul class="rules_1">
      <% l.choose.forEach(function (item) { %><li><%- item %></li><% }); %>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section_2 article_1__section" id="int" aria-labelledby="int-heading">
    <h2 class="section_2__h1" id="int-heading"><%= l.intTitle %></h2>
    <p class="article_1__p"><%- l.intLead %></p>
    <section class="table_3" tabindex="0" aria-label="<%= l.intTableLabel %>">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><% l.intHead.forEach(function (h) { %><th scope="col"><%= h %></th><% }); %></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <% l.intRows.forEach(function (row) { %>
            <tr><th scope="row"><%= row[0] %></th><% row.slice(1).forEach(function (cell) { %><td><%= cell %></td><% }); %></tr>
          <% }); %>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>
    <h3 class="section_2__h2"><%= l.intClipsTitle %></h3>
    <ol class="steps_1">
      <% l.intClips.forEach(function (step) { %><li><%- step %></li><% }); %>
    </ol>
    <h3 class="section_2__h2"><%= l.intRecTitle %></h3>
    <ol class="steps_1">
      <% l.intRec.forEach(function (step) { %><li><%- step %></li><% }); %>
    </ol>
    <p class="article_1__p"><%- l.intClipsWhy %></p>
    <h3 class="section_2__h2"><%= l.intControllerTitle %></h3>
    <ol class="steps_1">
      <% l.intController.forEach(function (step) { %><li><%- step %></li><% }); %>
    </ol>
    <%- include("_mock", { mock: l.intMock }) %>
    <% l.anyWhy.forEach(function (text) { %><p class="article_1__p"><%- text %></p><% }); %>
    <h3 class="section_2__h2"><%= l.intMenuTitle %></h3>
    <p class="article_1__p"><%- l.intMenuLead %></p>
    <ol class="steps_1">
      <% l.intMenu.forEach(function (step) { %><li><%- step %></li><% }); %>
    </ol>
    <%- include("_mock", { mock: l.intMenuMock }) %>
    <% l.intMenuHow.forEach(function (text) { %><p class="article_1__p"><%- text %></p><% }); %>
  </section>

  <section class="section_2 article_1__section" id="float" aria-labelledby="float-heading">
    <h2 class="section_2__h1" id="float-heading"><%= l.floatTitle %></h2>
    <p class="article_1__p"><%- l.floatLead %></p>
    <ol class="route_1">
      <% l.floatRoute.forEach(function (step) { %>
        <li class="route_1__step"><span class="route_1__head"><%= step.head %></span><span class="route_1__note"><%= step.note %></span></li>
      <% }); %>
    </ol>
    <h3 class="section_2__h2"><%= l.floatStateTitle %></h3>
    <ol class="steps_1">
      <% l.floatState.forEach(function (step) { %><li><%- step %></li><% }); %>
    </ol>
    <%- include("_mock", { mock: l.floatMock }) %>
    <h3 class="section_2__h2"><%= l.floatClipsTitle %></h3>
    <ol class="steps_1">
      <% l.floatClips.forEach(function (step) { %><li><%- step %></li><% }); %>
    </ol>
    <p class="article_1__p"><%- l.floatColor %></p>
    <h3 class="section_2__h2"><%= l.floatMenuTitle %></h3>
    <ol class="steps_1">
      <% l.floatMenu.forEach(function (step) { %><li><%- step %></li><% }); %>
    </ol>
    <h3 class="section_2__h2"><%= l.btTitle %></h3>
    <p class="article_1__p"><%= l.btLead %></p>
    <ol class="steps_1">
      <% l.bt.forEach(function (step) { %><li><%- step %></li><% }); %>
    </ol>
    <% l.btWhen.forEach(function (text) { %><p class="article_1__p"><%- text %></p><% }); %>
  </section>

  <section class="section_2 article_1__section" id="demo" aria-labelledby="demo-heading">
    <h2 class="section_2__h1" id="demo-heading"><%= l.demoTitle %></h2>
    <p class="article_1__p"><%= l.demoLead %></p>
    <div class="demo_2 js_radial_demo" data-frames="60"
      data-frame="<%= d.frame %>" data-size="<%= d.size %>" data-color="<%= d.color %>" data-remote="<%= d.remote %>">
      <div class="demo_2__faces">
        <div class="demo_2__face">
          <p class="demo_2__who"><%= d.look %></p>
          <div class="js_radial_look"><%- hat(v0, "size") %></div>
        </div>
        <div class="demo_2__face">
          <p class="demo_2__who"><%= d.clip %></p>
          <div class="js_radial_clip"><%- timeline(v0) %></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="demo_2__controls">
        <div class="demo_1__range">
          <p class="demo_1__label"><label for="radial-value"><%= d.slider %></label> <output class="demo_1__value" for="radial-value"><%= v0.toFixed(2) %></output></p>
          <input type="range" min="0" max="100" step="1" value="<%= v0 * 100 %>" id="radial-value" class="js_radial_value">
        </div>
        <fieldset class="demo_1__distance">
          <legend class="demo_1__label"><%= d.mode %></legend>
          <% d.modes.forEach(function (m, i) { %>
            <label><input type="radio" name="radial-mode" value="<%= m.value %>" class="js_radial_mode"<% if (i === 0) { %> checked<% } %>> <%= m.text %></label>
          <% }); %>
        </fieldset>
      </div>
      <div class="demo_2__output" aria-live="polite">
        <p class="demo_1__why js_radial_why"><%= fill(d.frame, { v: v0.toFixed(2), f: Math.round(v0 * FRAMES) }) %></p>
        <p class="demo_1__result js_radial_result"><%= fill(d.size, { x: (0.5 + v0).toFixed(2) }) %></p>
        <p class="demo_1__why js_radial_remote"><%= fill(d.remote, { r: remote(v0).toFixed(3) }) %></p>
      </div>
      <noscript><p class="section_2__note"><%= d.noJs %></p></noscript>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section_2 article_1__section" id="sync" aria-labelledby="sync-heading">
    <h2 class="section_2__h1" id="sync-heading"><%= l.syncTitle %></h2>
    <% l.sync.forEach(function (text) { %><p class="article_1__p"><%- text %></p><% }); %>
    <section class="table_3" tabindex="0" aria-label="<%= l.bitsTableLabel %>">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><% l.bitsHead.forEach(function (h) { %><th scope="col"><%= h %></th><% }); %></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <% l.bitsRows.forEach(function (row) { %>
            <tr><th scope="row"><%= row[0] %></th><td><%= row[1] %></td><td><%= row[2] %></td></tr>
          <% }); %>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>
    <ul class="rules_1">
      <% l.bits.forEach(function (item) { %><li><%- item %></li><% }); %>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section_2 article_1__section" id="cases" aria-labelledby="cases-heading">
    <h2 class="section_2__h1" id="cases-heading"><%= l.casesTitle %></h2>
    <div class="case_1">
      <% l.cases.forEach(function (c) { %>
        <section class="case_1__item">
          <h3 class="case_1__title"><%= c.title %></h3>
          <dl class="case_1__list">
            <div><dt><%= l.caseLabels.symptom %></dt><dd><%= c.symptom %></dd></div>
            <div><dt><%= l.caseLabels.cause %></dt><dd><%= c.cause %></dd></div>
            <div><dt><%= l.caseLabels.fix %></dt><dd><%= c.fix %></dd></div>
          </dl>
        </section>
      <% }); %>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section_2 article_1__section" id="care" aria-labelledby="care-heading">
    <h2 class="section_2__h1" id="care-heading"><%= l.careTitle %></h2>
    <ul class="rules_1">
      <% l.care.forEach(function (item) { %><li><%= item %></li><% }); %>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section_2 article_1__section" id="summary" aria-labelledby="summary-heading">
    <h2 class="section_2__h1" id="summary-heading"><%= l.sumTitle %></h2>
    <ul class="rules_1">
      <% l.sum.forEach(function (item) { %><li><%= item %></li><% }); %>
    </ul>
    <p class="article_1__p"><%- l.next %></p>
    <p class="section_2__more"><a href="<%= prefix %>/avatar-tips/"><%= l.back %></a></p>
  </section>
</article>
